---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ArticleEndNote from "@/components/ArticleEndNote.astro";
import "@/styles/services.css";
const title = "GeM Seller Registration: A Practical Starting Guide";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description="Understand GeM seller registration, catalogue preparation and bid readiness. Official resources and independent support for Tamil Nadu MSMEs." article={{ headline: title, publishDate: "2026-09-24", section: "GeM guides" }} breadcrumbs={[{ name: "Home", path: "/" }, { name: "GeM services", path: "/gem-services/" }, { name: "Seller registration guide", path: "/guides/gem-seller-registration/" }]}>
  <article class="service-page">
    <header class="service-intro"><div class="wrap"><nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/gem-services/">GeM services</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span>Registration guide</span></nav><h1>How to approach GeM seller registration.</h1><p class="intro-copy">Start on the official Government e-Marketplace at <a href="https://gem.gov.in/">gem.gov.in</a>. Registration, catalogue management and bidding are distinct parts of the seller journey.</p><p class="fine">By Porul.in · <time datetime="2026-09-24">24 September 2026</time> · Service guide</p></div></header>
    <div class="wrap">
      <section class="service-band"><h2>1. Establish who will manage the account</h2><p>Use an authorised representative of the business and contact details the business controls. Keep access and approvals with your business, even when a consultant helps prepare information.</p><p>GeM's seller training includes a registration and account-management course. Use its current instructions alongside the live portal, because required fields and verification steps can change.</p></section>
      <section class="service-band"><h2>2. Organise your business information</h2><p>Before asking for assistance, identify your business type, products or services and any existing GeM account. Keep your business-registration, tax and MSME records accessible where applicable. Check the live portal for the exact records required for your situation; a general checklist cannot establish eligibility.</p><p>For an initial Porul enquiry, a description of your business and the problem is enough. Do not email identity documents, bank records, passwords or OTPs.</p></section>
      <section class="service-band"><h2>3. Prepare the catalogue separately</h2><p>Account setup is only the start. Listing a product requires working through its category and the information requested there. Gather accurate specifications, product images, brand information and the number of items you want to list.</p><p>If a catalogue has been rejected, start with the exact rejection message. Category fit, missing information and approval requirements should be checked against the current portal, rather than repeatedly submitting an unchanged listing.</p></section>
      <section class="service-band"><h2>4. Review each bid before participating</h2><p>A registered account does not prove that you qualify for a particular bid. Read the bid document and amendments, compare the requirements with your business records and confirm that you can meet the commercial and delivery obligations.</p><p>For help with a specific opportunity, send its official link or ID and closing date. A useful review should establish missing evidence and whether there is enough time to prepare the submission.</p></section>
      <section class="service-band"><h2>GeM and Tamil Nadu eProcurement are separate</h2><p>The Tamil Nadu eProcurement portal has its own bidder enrolment and submission process. Its official bidder resources cover registration, document uploads, bid covers and BOQ preparation. A GeM account is not a substitute for completing the steps on the portal publishing your tender.</p></section>
      <section class="service-band"><h2>Official resources</h2><ul><li><a href="https://gem.gov.in/">Government e-Marketplace: official portal</a></li><li><a href="https://elearning.gem.gov.in/course/index.php?categoryid=2">GeM seller courses: registration, catalogues, bids and order fulfilment</a></li><li><a href="https://tntenders.gov.in/nicgep/app">Tamil Nadu eProcurement portal</a></li><li><a href="https://www.tntenders.gov.in/nicgep/app?page=BiddersManualKit&amp;service=page">Tamil Nadu official bidder manuals</a></li></ul><p class="fine">This guide explains the starting workflow. The current official portal, bid documents and amendments govern the requirements for your case.</p></section>
      <section class="service-band"><h2>Need someone to help with the work?</h2><p>Porul.in provides independent GeM registration and catalogue assistance for Tamil Nadu MSMEs, with Shreepriya handling GeM portal work. We review your requirement before agreeing a scope and fee.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button button--dark" href="/enquire/?service=registration">Enquire about registration →</a><a href="/gem-services/">Explore GeM services</a></div><p class="fine">This is Porul's service guide. Porul is not affiliated with GeM or the government. Paid assistance does not guarantee approval or a contract. For corrections, email <a href="mailto:hello@porul.in?subject=GeM%20guide%20correction">hello@porul.in</a>.</p></section>
      <ArticleEndNote />
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
